{"\ufeffEmployee Leave Management (ELM)\nUse Case Specifications \u2014 Final Synchronized v1.4\nFusion ERP \u2022 Employee Leave Management \u2022 Synchronized baseline v1.4\nUse-case convention\nELM uses one use-case formalism with two types: Actor-triggered and Event-triggered. For an event-triggered UC, Primary Actor is \u201cN.A. \u2014 Event-triggered\u201d": null, " the initiating time/external event is stated in Trigger. ELM itself is not its own UC actor. Supporting Actors/Systems list only genuine external participants or recipients.\n1. Use Case Registry\nUC ID\nUse Case Name\nPrimary Actor\nStatus\nPrimary CFRs\nUC Type\nEL-UC-001\nApply for Leave\nEmployee\nActive\nCFR-EL-002\u2013003, CFR-EL-011, CFR-EL-015\nActor-triggered\nEL-UC-002\nRespond to Substitute Request\nSubstitute / Responsibility Holder\nActive\nCFR-EL-012, CFR-EL-030\nActor-triggered\nEL-UC-003\nReview Leave-Related Request at Unit Head\nUnit Head\nActive\nCFR-EL-013\u2013016, CFR-EL-019\u2013020\nActor-triggered\nEL-UC-004\nVerify and Route Higher-Sanction Request\nDeputy Registrar (Estt.) / Establishment Processing Role\nActive\nCFR-EL-014, CFR-EL-019\u2013020\nActor-triggered\nEL-UC-005\nMake Final Sanctioning Decision\nSanctioning Authority (Deputy Registrar (Estt.), Dean, Registrar, Director, or other configured competent authority)\nActive\nCFR-EL-006, CFR-EL-014\u2013016, CFR-EL-019\u2013020\nActor-triggered\nEL-UC-007\nWithdraw Pending Request\nEmployee\nActive\nCFR-EL-017\u2013018\nActor-triggered\nEL-UC-008\nRequest Cancellation of Approved Leave\nEmployee\nActive\nCFR-EL-019\nActor-triggered\nEL-UC-009\nRequest Extension of Ongoing Leave\nEmployee\nActive\nCFR-EL-020\nActor-triggered\nEL-UC-010\nSubmit Resumption of Duty\nEmployee\nActive\nCFR-EL-021\nActor-triggered\nEL-UC-011\nReview Resumption\nApplicable Sanctioning Authority\nActive\nCFR-EL-021\nActor-triggered\nEL-UC-012\nView Leave Balances and History\nEmployee\nActive\nCFR-EL-016, CFR-EL-022\nActor-triggered\nEL-UC-013\nObtain Printable/Exportable Leave Application\nEmployee\nActive\nCFR-EL-023\nActor-triggered\nEL-UC-014\nMaintain Policy and Hierarchy Configuration\nAuthorized administrative role\nActive\nCFR-EL-024\nActor-triggered\nEL-UC-015\nMaintain and Publish Holiday/RH Calendar\nAuthorized administrative role\nActive\nCFR-EL-005, CFR-EL-025\nActor-triggered\nEL-UC-016\nRecord Already-Sanctioned Offline Leave\nLeave Administrator\nActive\nCFR-EL-027\nActor-triggered\nEL-UC-017\nMaintain Authorized Leave Records\nAuthorized administrative role\nActive\nCFR-EL-026\nActor-triggered\nEL-UC-018\nConfigure Workflow SLA Thresholds\nAuthorized administrative role\nActive\nCFR-EL-029\nActor-triggered\nEL-UC-019\nNominate Replacement Substitute After Decline\nEmployee\nActive\nCFR-EL-011\u2013012, CFR-EL-018\nActor-triggered\nEL-UC-020\nExecute Year-End Leave Processing\nN.A. \u2014 Event-triggered\nActive\nCFR-EL-004\u2013009, CFR-EL-028\nEvent-triggered\nEL-UC-021\nProcess SLA Threshold Event\nN.A. \u2014 Event-triggered\nActive\nCFR-EL-031\u2013032\nEvent-triggered\nEL-UC-006\nModify Pending Request\nEmployee\nRETIRED\nSuperseded by CFR-EL-017 / BR-EL-034\nRetired\n\n2. Use Case Specifications\nEL-UC-001 \u2014 Apply for Leave\nPrimary Actor\nEmployee\nSupporting Actors / Systems\nAcademic Calendar service (for VL vacation-period data)": null, " Substitute interaction is handled by EL-UC-002 when required.\nGoal / Description\nCreate and submit a valid new leave application and place it into the applicable processing path.\nTrigger\nEmployee needs to request CL, RH, SCL, EL, COL, or VL.\nPreconditions\n\u2022 Employee is authenticated and authorized for own leave activity.\n\u2022 Current configured leave policy/hierarchy is available": null, " effective published holiday/RH calendar is available": null, " Academic Calendar vacation-period data is available where VL is requested.\nUC Type\nActor-triggered\n\nMain Success Scenario\nM1. Employee starts a new leave application.\nM2. Employee selects the leave category and requested period and enters purpose/reason and other required information.\nM3. System captures Station Leave details in the same application when applicable.\nM4. System validates category eligibility, entitlement/balance, counting/calendar conditions, and impermissible overlap.\nM5. When responsibility coverage is required, Employee nominates one eligible substitute.\nM6. Employee submits the application.\nM7. If substitute consent is required, System places the request in Awaiting Substitute Response": null, " otherwise it routes the request to Unit Head review. A Director-applicant follows the self-sanction path.\nAlternative / Exception Flows\nA1 Validation fails: identify the failed condition and do not allow progression.\nA2 Substitute nomination invalid: reject the nominee and allow another eligible nominee.\nA3 After a substitute decline, the Employee may invoke EL-UC-019 to nominate a replacement or EL-UC-007 to withdraw.\nSuccess Postcondition\nA valid submitted request exists in the correct next processing state.\nFailure / Minimal Guarantee\nNo invalid request is allowed to progress": null, " previously entered data may remain available as implementation permits.\nRelated Business Rules\nBR-EL-001\u2013015, BR-EL-020, BR-EL-030\u2013031, BR-EL-036\nRelated Functional Requirements\nCFR-EL-002\u2013003, CFR-EL-011, CFR-EL-015\nRelated Workflow(s)\nCW-EL-01\n\nEL-UC-002 \u2014 Respond to Substitute Request\nPrimary Actor\nSubstitute / Responsibility Holder\nSupporting Actors / Systems\nEmployee\nGoal / Description\nAccept or decline a nominated responsibility assignment.\nTrigger\nA substitute responsibility request is assigned to the nominated employee.\nPreconditions\n\u2022 The nominee is an eligible substitute for the responsibility period.\n\u2022 The associated leave/extension request is awaiting substitute response.\nUC Type\nActor-triggered\n\nMain Success Scenario\nM1. Substitute opens the assigned responsibility request.\nM2. System presents the applicant, responsibility period, and relevant request context.\nM3. Substitute selects Accept or Decline.\nM4. System records the response.\nM5. If Accept, the consent gate is released and the request proceeds to Unit Head review": null, " if Decline, the request becomes Applicant Action Required.\nAlternative / Exception Flows\nA1 If the request is no longer pending, System prevents a stale response.\nSuccess Postcondition\nThe substitute response is recorded and the request enters the outcome-appropriate state.\nFailure / Minimal Guarantee\nNo routing occurs without a valid recorded response.\nRelated Business Rules\nBR-EL-014\u2013015, BR-EL-035\u2013036\nRelated Functional Requirements\nCFR-EL-012, CFR-EL-030\nRelated Workflow(s)\nCW-EL-01": null, " CW-EL-03\n\nEL-UC-003 \u2014 Review Leave-Related Request at Unit Head\nPrimary Actor\nUnit Head\nSupporting Actors / Systems\nEmployee": null, " Establishment / final Sanctioning Authority as downstream roles\nGoal / Description\nReview a routed new-leave, cancellation, or extension request and record the decision/recommendation permitted by the applicable policy.\nTrigger\nA request enters the Unit Head work queue.\nPreconditions\n\u2022 The request has passed applicable submission/consent gates.\n\u2022 The Unit Head is the resolved Unit Head for the applicant.\nUC Type\nActor-triggered\n\nMain Success Scenario\nM1. Unit Head opens the assigned request and reviews the request context and available supporting information.\nM2. For a new CL/RH request, Unit Head records final Approve or Reject.\nM3. For higher-sanction new leave, cancellation of higher-sanction leave, or EL/COL/VL extension, Unit Head records Recommended or Not Recommended.\nM4. System records the outcome.\nM5. A Unit-Head-final outcome completes the decision": null, " a recommendation outcome continues through the configured higher-sanction path.\nAlternative / Exception Flows\nA1 Director-applicant cases do not use the normal Unit Head path.\nA2 Not Recommended for higher-sanction contexts is not a final rejection.\nSuccess Postcondition\nThe Unit Head outcome is recorded and the request is either finally decided or advanced to the configured next stage.\nFailure / Minimal Guarantee\nNo unauthorized or out-of-scope decision is recorded.\nRelated Business Rules\nBR-EL-016\u2013020, BR-EL-023, BR-EL-025, BR-EL-030, BR-EL-036\nRelated Functional Requirements\nCFR-EL-013\u2013016, CFR-EL-019\u2013020\nRelated Workflow(s)\nCW-EL-01": null, " CW-EL-02": null, " CW-EL-03\n\nEL-UC-004 \u2014 Verify and Route Higher-Sanction Request\nPrimary Actor\nDeputy Registrar (Estt.) / Establishment Processing Role\nSupporting Actors / Systems\nUnit Head": null, " final Sanctioning Authority\nGoal / Description\nPerform the configured Establishment-level verification/routing step and forward the request to the resolved competent authority.\nTrigger\nA higher-sanction request reaches an Establishment step that is configured for its path.\nPreconditions\n\u2022 An Establishment step is configured for this request context.\n\u2022 The required upstream review/consent outcome has been recorded.\nUC Type\nActor-triggered\n\nMain Success Scenario\nM1. Establishment opens the routed work item.\nM2. System presents the request and resolved routing context.\nM3. Establishment performs the configured verification/routing checks.\nM4. System resolves/validates the next competent authority using current hierarchy configuration.\nM5. Establishment forwards the request to the resolved final Sanctioning Authority.\nAlternative / Exception Flows\nA1 If no Establishment step is configured, this use case is bypassed.\nA2 If routing context is inconsistent or incomplete, do not forward until the inconsistency is resolved through authorized configuration/record handling.\nSuccess Postcondition\nThe request is assigned to the resolved final Sanctioning Authority.\nFailure / Minimal Guarantee\nThe request is not forwarded to an unauthorized/unresolved authority.\nRelated Business Rules\nBR-EL-018\u2013019, BR-EL-023, BR-EL-025, BR-EL-030, BR-EL-036\nRelated Functional Requirements\nCFR-EL-014, CFR-EL-019\u2013020\nRelated Workflow(s)\nCW-EL-01": null, " CW-EL-03\n\nEL-UC-005 \u2014 Make Final Sanctioning Decision\nPrimary Actor\nSanctioning Authority (Deputy Registrar (Estt.), Dean, Registrar, Director, or other configured competent authority)\nSupporting Actors / Systems\nEmployee": null, " Unit Head": null, " Establishment where configured\nGoal / Description\nRecord the final approve/reject decision for a routed higher-sanction new-leave, cancellation, or extension request.\nTrigger\nA request is assigned to the resolved final Sanctioning Authority.\nPreconditions\n\u2022 The actor is the resolved competent final authority for the request.\n\u2022 Required upstream routing and consent gates have been completed.\nUC Type\nActor-triggered\n\nMain Success Scenario\nM1. Authority opens the assigned request and reviews the request, recommendation, and available evidence.\nM2. Authority records Approve or Reject.\nM3. System records the final decision and notifies the employee.\nM4. For new-leave approval, System updates the leave record/account.\nM5. For cancellation approval, System marks the leave Cancelled and restores/adjusts deducted balance": null, " cancellation rejection preserves the original approval.\nM6. For extension approval, System posts only the incremental additional period": null, " extension rejection preserves the original approved leave.\nAlternative / Exception Flows\nA1 SCL purpose admissibility is decided by the applicable Sanctioning Authority": null, " no separate encoded admissibility criterion is required.\nA2 Director-as-applicant uses the Director-specific self-sanction path.\nSuccess Postcondition\nA final decision and the context-appropriate completion effects are recorded.\nFailure / Minimal Guarantee\nNo final decision is recorded by an unauthorized authority.\nRelated Business Rules\nBR-EL-004, BR-EL-017\u2013020, BR-EL-023\u2013025, BR-EL-030, BR-EL-036\nRelated Functional Requirements\nCFR-EL-006, CFR-EL-014\u2013016, CFR-EL-019\u2013020\nRelated Workflow(s)\nCW-EL-01": null, " CW-EL-03\n\nEL-UC-007 \u2014 Withdraw Pending Request\nPrimary Actor\nEmployee\nSupporting Actors / Systems\nConcerned processing/sanctioning roles\nGoal / Description\nImmediately terminate a pending request before final approval.\nTrigger\nEmployee chooses to withdraw a request that is still pending before final approval.\nPreconditions\n\u2022 The request is pending and has not received final approval.\nUC Type\nActor-triggered\n\nMain Success Scenario\nM1. Employee selects the pending request and confirms withdrawal.\nM2. System validates that final approval has not occurred.\nM3. System makes the withdrawal effective immediately.\nM4. System terminates all remaining approval processing, prevents later approve/reject actions, and notifies concerned roles.\nAlternative / Exception Flows\nA1 If final approval already exists, withdrawal is unavailable": null, " approved-leave cancellation applies where its preconditions hold.\nSuccess Postcondition\nRequest is Withdrawn and no remaining approval action can be taken.\nFailure / Minimal Guarantee\nNo withdrawal is applied to an already finally approved request.\nRelated Business Rules\nBR-EL-022, BR-EL-034, BR-EL-036\nRelated Functional Requirements\nCFR-EL-017\u2013018\nRelated Workflow(s)\nCW-EL-01": null, " CW-EL-03 (only when the extension request itself is pending and withdrawal is applicable)\n\nEL-UC-008 \u2014 Request Cancellation of Approved Leave\nPrimary Actor\nEmployee\nSupporting Actors / Systems\nUnit Head": null, " Establishment where configured": null, " final Sanctioning Authority\nGoal / Description\nRequest pre-start cancellation of an approved leave without editing the approved leave in place.\nTrigger\nEmployee needs to reverse an approved leave before its approved start date.\nPreconditions\n\u2022 Leave is finally Approved.\n\u2022 Approved start date has not yet occurred.\nUC Type\nActor-triggered\n\nMain Success Scenario\nM1. Employee selects the approved leave and requests cancellation.\nM2. System validates that the leave has not started and that withdrawal is no longer the applicable mechanism.\nM3. System creates the cancellation request without editing the approved leave.\nM4. System routes the cancellation to the Unit Head and then through the same applicable hierarchy as the original leave.\nAlternative / Exception Flows\nA1 If leave has started, cancellation is unavailable": null, " extension/resumption applies as relevant.\nA2 If cancellation is finally rejected, original approved leave remains unchanged.\nA3 If cancellation is approved and revised leave is still needed, Employee submits a fresh leave application.\nSuccess Postcondition\nA valid cancellation request enters the applicable decision path.\nFailure / Minimal Guarantee\nNo pre-start cancellation request is created outside its eligibility boundary.\nRelated Business Rules\nBR-EL-023\u2013024, BR-EL-030, BR-EL-036\nRelated Functional Requirements\nCFR-EL-019\nRelated Workflow(s)\nCW-EL-02\n\nEL-UC-009 \u2014 Request Extension of Ongoing Leave\nPrimary Actor\nEmployee\nSupporting Actors / Systems\nSubstitute": null, " final Sanctioning Authority\nGoal / Description\nRequest additional leave time while ongoing EL, COL, or VL is being availed.\nTrigger\nEmployee on ongoing EL/COL/VL needs additional leave time.\nPreconditions\n\u2022 Original leave is ongoing and is EL, COL, or VL.\nUC Type\nActor-triggered\n\nMain Success Scenario\nM1. Employee enters the requested additional period and required information.\nM2. System validates eligibility, balance, calendar/counting conditions and other applicable rules.\nM3. When responsibility coverage is required, Employee nominates an eligible substitute and obtains consent through EL-UC-002.\nM4. System creates the extension request and routes it to Unit Head review and the configured higher-sanction path.\nAlternative / Exception Flows\nA1 Validation failure prevents the extension request from progressing.\nA2 Substitute decline invokes replacement handling through EL-UC-019": null, " no approval routing occurs before required acceptance.\nSuccess Postcondition\nA valid extension request enters the applicable higher-sanction path.\nFailure / Minimal Guarantee\nOriginal approved leave remains unaffected by an invalid/unsubmitted extension request.\nRelated Business Rules\nBR-EL-001, BR-EL-005\u2013015, BR-EL-017\u2013019, BR-EL-025, BR-EL-030\u2013031, BR-EL-036\nRelated Functional Requirements\nCFR-EL-020\nRelated Workflow(s)\nCW-EL-03\n\nEL-UC-010 \u2014 Submit Resumption of Duty\nPrimary Actor\nEmployee\nSupporting Actors / Systems\nApplicable Sanctioning Authority\nGoal / Description\nSubmit actual return-to-duty information after EL, COL, or VL for review.\nTrigger\nEmployee returns to duty after EL/COL/VL.\nPreconditions\n\u2022 An EL/COL/VL leave record exists for the employee.\n\u2022 Employee has returned and can state the actual resumption date.\nUC Type\nActor-triggered\n\nMain Success Scenario\nM1. Employee opens the relevant leave record.\nM2. Employee enters actual resumption date and required resumption details.\nM3. System records the resumption submission and routes it to the applicable Sanctioning Authority for review.\nAlternative / Exception Flows\nA1 Resumption is outside this baseline for CL/RH/SCL as a formal reviewed process.\nSuccess Postcondition\nA resumption submission exists in Resumption Review Pending.\nFailure / Minimal Guarantee\nNo review submission is created if required information is missing/invalid.\nRelated Business Rules\nBR-EL-027, BR-EL-036\nRelated Functional Requirements\nCFR-EL-021\nRelated Workflow(s)\nCW-EL-04\n\nEL-UC-011 \u2014 Review Resumption\nPrimary Actor\nApplicable Sanctioning Authority\nSupporting Actors / Systems\nEmployee": null, " leave/attendance records\nGoal / Description\nReview the submitted resumption and apply only the adjustments required by the actual return date.\nTrigger\nA resumption submission is assigned for review.\nPreconditions\n\u2022 A valid resumption submission exists for EL/COL/VL.\n\u2022 Actor is the applicable Sanctioning Authority.\nUC Type\nActor-triggered\n\nMain Success Scenario\nM1. Authority reviews the submitted actual resumption date/details.\nM2. System compares actual resumption date with approved end date.\nM3. If dates match, Authority records review completion": null, " no approved leave-period or balance adjustment is made.\nM4. If actual date is earlier or later, Authority confirms the review outcome and System records actual leave period, adjusts balance accordingly, and synchronizes relevant leave/attendance records.\nAlternative / Exception Flows\nA1 No generic 'close leave' state transition is asserted for normal resumption in this baseline.\nSuccess Postcondition\nResumption review is recorded": null, " early/late return produces the required data/balance synchronization.\nFailure / Minimal Guarantee\nNo balance/period adjustment is applied before required review.\nRelated Business Rules\nBR-EL-027\u2013028, BR-EL-036\nRelated Functional Requirements\nCFR-EL-021\nRelated Workflow(s)\nCW-EL-04\n\nEL-UC-012 \u2014 View Leave Balances and History\nPrimary Actor\nEmployee\nSupporting Actors / Systems\nNone\nGoal / Description\nInspect own current leave balances and leave-account/request history, including request status and final decisions.\nTrigger\nEmployee wants to inspect current balances or historical/request status information.\nPreconditions\n\u2022 Employee is authenticated and authorized to access own leave information.\nUC Type\nActor-triggered\n\nMain Success Scenario\nM1. Employee opens leave balance/history inquiry.\nM2. System displays current leave balances.\nM3. System displays accessible leave-account/request history including current request status and recorded final decisions.\nSuccess Postcondition\nRequested balance/history information is displayed.\nFailure / Minimal Guarantee\nNo other employee's protected leave information is exposed.\nRelated Business Rules\nBR-EL-036\nRelated Functional Requirements\nCFR-EL-016, CFR-EL-022\nRelated Workflow(s)\nN/A\n\nEL-UC-013 \u2014 Obtain Printable/Exportable Leave Application\nPrimary Actor\nEmployee\nSupporting Actors / Systems\nNone\nGoal / Description\nObtain a printable or exportable representation of an accessible leave application.\nTrigger\nEmployee needs a printable/exportable copy of an accessible leave application.\nPreconditions\n\u2022 Employee is authorized to access the application.\nUC Type\nActor-triggered\n\nMain Success Scenario\nM1. Employee selects an accessible leave application.\nM2. Employee requests print/export representation.\nM3. System produces the representation for the selected application.\nSuccess Postcondition\nPrintable/exportable representation is available.\nFailure / Minimal Guarantee\nNo representation is produced for an application the employee is not authorized to access.\nRelated Business Rules\nBR-EL-036\nRelated Functional Requirements\nCFR-EL-023\nRelated Workflow(s)\nN/A\n\nEL-UC-014 \u2014 Maintain Policy and Hierarchy Configuration\nPrimary Actor\nAuthorized administrative role\nSupporting Actors / Systems\nNone\nGoal / Description\nCreate/revise current ELM leave-policy parameters and maintain hierarchy configuration used for validation and routing.\nTrigger\nAuthorized administrator needs to change current ELM policy or hierarchy configuration.\nPreconditions\n\u2022 Actor is authorized for the relevant configuration capability.\nUC Type\nActor-triggered\n\nMain Success Scenario\nM1. Administrator opens the relevant configuration.\nM2. Administrator creates/revises policy parameters and/or hierarchy configuration.\nM3. System validates the configuration input and saves it as the current configured value.\nM4. Subsequent validation/routing uses the current configured values.\nAlternative / Exception Flows\nA1 This baseline has no policy draft/publish/effective-version lifecycle": null, " do not create unpublished policy versions.\nSuccess Postcondition\nCurrent ELM policy/hierarchy configuration is updated.\nFailure / Minimal Guarantee\nUnauthorized or invalid configuration changes are not applied.\nRelated Business Rules\nBR-EL-030, BR-EL-036\nRelated Functional Requirements\nCFR-EL-024\nRelated Workflow(s)\nN/A\n\nEL-UC-015 \u2014 Maintain and Publish Holiday/RH Calendar\nPrimary Actor\nAuthorized administrative role\nSupporting Actors / Systems\nNone\nGoal / Description\nCreate, revise, and publish the holiday/RH calendar used by date and RH validation.\nTrigger\nAuthorized administrator needs to create or replace the ELM holiday/RH calendar.\nPreconditions\n\u2022 Actor is authorized to maintain the holiday/RH calendar.\nUC Type\nActor-triggered\n\nMain Success Scenario\nM1. Administrator creates or revises the calendar.\nM2. System validates calendar data.\nM3. Administrator publishes the replacement calendar.\nM4. System makes the published calendar effective for subsequent date/RH validation.\nAlternative / Exception Flows\nA1 Until a replacement is published, the currently effective published calendar remains governing.\nSuccess Postcondition\nA valid published holiday/RH calendar is effective.\nFailure / Minimal Guarantee\nUnpublished/invalid replacement data does not displace the current effective published calendar.\nRelated Business Rules\nBR-EL-003, BR-EL-031, BR-EL-036\nRelated Functional Requirements\nCFR-EL-005, CFR-EL-025\nRelated Workflow(s)\nN/A\n\nEL-UC-016 \u2014 Record Already-Sanctioned Offline Leave\nPrimary Actor\nLeave Administrator\nSupporting Actors / Systems\nNone\nGoal / Description\nSynchronize ELM with leave already sanctioned through an authorized offline/paper process when ELM could not originally be used.\nTrigger\nAuthorized administrator needs to record already-sanctioned leave that was handled offline for an acceptable reason.\nPreconditions\n\u2022 Leave was already validly sanctioned through an authorized offline/paper process.\n\u2022 Actor is authorized to perform retrospective synchronization.\nUC Type\nActor-triggered\n\nMain Success Scenario\nM1. Administrator identifies the employee and sanctioned leave.\nM2. Administrator enters the sanctioned leave details and sanction/reference evidence.\nM3. System validates the entry for record consistency.\nM4. System records the leave and updates relevant leave balance/history.\nM5. System does not create a second approval workflow.\nAlternative / Exception Flows\nA1 If sanction/reference evidence or record-consistency validation is insufficient, do not complete synchronization.\nSuccess Postcondition\nELM records reflect the already-sanctioned leave without a new sanction decision.\nFailure / Minimal Guarantee\nNo unsanctioned retrospective leave is turned into an approval through this capability.\nRelated Business Rules\nBR-EL-029, BR-EL-036\u2013037\nRelated Functional Requirements\nCFR-EL-027\nRelated Workflow(s)\nN/A\n\nEL-UC-017 \u2014 Maintain Authorized Leave Records\nPrimary Actor\nAuthorized administrative role\nSupporting Actors / Systems\nNone\nGoal / Description\nMaintain or correct leave records within the actor's authorized record-maintenance scope without creating a sanctioning decision.\nTrigger\nAuthorized administrator needs to perform permitted leave-record maintenance/correction.\nPreconditions\n\u2022 Actor has the relevant record-maintenance authorization.\nUC Type\nActor-triggered\n\nMain Success Scenario\nM1. Administrator selects the relevant leave record.\nM2. Administrator performs an authorized maintenance/correction action.\nM3. System validates authorization and record consistency.\nM4. System saves the permitted record change and preserves audit/history as implemented.\nAlternative / Exception Flows\nA1 If the attempted change would constitute a new sanctioning decision, this maintenance use case must not be used.\nSuccess Postcondition\nAuthorized record maintenance is applied without creating a new leave approval/rejection.\nFailure / Minimal Guarantee\nUnauthorized or sanction-equivalent changes are blocked.\nRelated Business Rules\nBR-EL-036\u2013037\nRelated Functional Requirements\nCFR-EL-026\nRelated Workflow(s)\nN/A\n\nEL-UC-018 \u2014 Configure Workflow SLA Thresholds\nPrimary Actor\nAuthorized administrative role\nSupporting Actors / Systems\nNone\nGoal / Description\nConfigure reminder and escalation thresholds for SLA-controlled actionable workflow tasks.\nTrigger\nAuthorized administrator needs to establish or change SLA thresholds.\nPreconditions\n\u2022 Actor is authorized to configure SLA thresholds.\nUC Type\nActor-triggered\n\nMain Success Scenario\nM1. Administrator opens SLA configuration.\nM2. Administrator specifies reminder and escalation thresholds for applicable actionable task classes.\nM3. System validates and saves the configuration.\nM4. Subsequent event-triggered SLA processing uses the configured thresholds.\nSuccess Postcondition\nValid reminder/escalation thresholds are available to event-triggered SLA processing.\nFailure / Minimal Guarantee\nInvalid or unauthorized threshold changes are not applied.\nRelated Business Rules\nBR-EL-038, BR-EL-036\nRelated Functional Requirements\nCFR-EL-029\nRelated Workflow(s)\nN/A\n\nEL-UC-019 \u2014 Nominate Replacement Substitute After Decline\nPrimary Actor\nEmployee\nSupporting Actors / Systems\nSubstitute / Responsibility Holder\nGoal / Description\nRecover from a substitute decline by nominating one replacement eligible substitute.\nTrigger\nA nominated substitute declines and the request enters Applicant Action Required.\nPreconditions\n\u2022 The associated request remains pending.\n\u2022 Responsibility coverage is still required.\nUC Type\nActor-triggered\n\nMain Success Scenario\nM1. Employee chooses to replace the declined substitute.\nM2. Employee nominates one replacement.\nM3. System validates replacement eligibility.\nM4. System assigns a fresh substitute request and places the leave/extension request in Awaiting Substitute Response.\nAlternative / Exception Flows\nA1 Employee may instead withdraw the pending request where withdrawal is applicable.\nSuccess Postcondition\nA fresh substitute response is awaited for an eligible replacement.\nFailure / Minimal Guarantee\nAn ineligible replacement is not assigned.\nRelated Business Rules\nBR-EL-014\u2013015, BR-EL-022, BR-EL-036\nRelated Functional Requirements\nCFR-EL-011\u2013012, CFR-EL-018\nRelated Workflow(s)\nCW-EL-01": null, " CW-EL-03\n\n3. Retired Use Case\nUse Case\nEL-UC-006 \u2014 Modify Pending Request\nDisposition\nRETIRED\nReason\nThe adjudicated baseline prohibits in-place post-submission modification. Change before final approval is handled by immediate withdrawal followed, if needed, by a fresh application.\nReplacement semantics\nCFR-EL-017, CFR-EL-018": null, " BR-EL-034, BR-EL-022": null, " EL-UC-007 and EL-UC-001.\n\n4. Event-Triggered Use Cases\nEL-UC-020 \u2014 Execute Year-End Leave Processing\nUC Type\nEvent-triggered\nPrimary Actor\nN.A. \u2014 Event-triggered\nSupporting Actors / Systems\nNone\nGoal / Description\nApply the defined year-end leave-account outcomes and record the resulting processing evidence.\nTrigger\nConfigured year-end boundary reached.\nPreconditions\nCurrent leave accounts and the applicable leave-category rules are available.\nMain Success Scenario\n1. System identifies leave accounts/categories requiring year-end processing.\n2. System lapses unused CL/RH/SCL, converts unused faculty VL to EL including fractional conversion and no VL carry-forward, and carries forward EL/COL according to policy.\n3. System records the resulting leave-account transactions.\n4. System reports processing exceptions.\nAlternative / Exception Flows\nIf an account cannot be processed consistently, the system reports the exception rather than silently applying an uncertain result.\nSuccess Postcondition\nYear-end balances reflect the applicable category rules": null, " transactions are recorded and exceptions are reported.\nFailure / Minimal Guarantee\nNo unvalidated/ambiguous year-end adjustment is silently committed.\nRelated Business Rules\nBR-EL-002\u2013009\nRelated Functional Requirements\nCFR-EL-004\u2013009, CFR-EL-028\nRelated Workflow(s)\nN/A \u2014 this event-triggered UC is an isolated year-end system operation, not by itself a connected multi-step business progression.\n\nEL-UC-021 \u2014 Process SLA Threshold Event\nUC Type\nEvent-triggered\nPrimary Actor\nN.A. \u2014 Event-triggered\nSupporting Actors / Systems\nResponsible user": null, " configured higher/responsible authority as notification/escalation recipient where applicable\nGoal / Description\nProcess a configured SLA reminder or escalation threshold for an actionable workflow task.\nTrigger\nConfigured reminder or escalation threshold reached for an actionable workflow task.\nPreconditions\nThe task is SLA-controlled and the applicable reminder/escalation thresholds are configured.\nMain Success Scenario\n1. System identifies the task and threshold event.\n2. System checks whether the task is still pending.\n3. At a reminder threshold, if still pending, System reminds the responsible user and logs the reminder.\n4. At an escalation threshold, if still pending, System performs the configured escalation action (notification and, where configured, routing/responsibility change) and logs the escalation.\n5. If the task is no longer pending, System issues no corresponding reminder/escalation.\nAlternative / Exception Flows\nNotification-only escalation does not create a workflow transition. Where configured escalation changes routing/responsibility, that automatic System transition is represented cross-cuttingly in the applicable workflow.\nSuccess Postcondition\nThe pending-only reminder/escalation rule is applied and any issued action is logged.\nFailure / Minimal Guarantee\nA completed/non-pending task is not reminded or escalated by the threshold event.\nRelated Business Rules\nBR-EL-032\u2013033, BR-EL-038\nRelated Functional Requirements\nCFR-EL-031\u2013032\nRelated Workflow(s)\nConditional cross-cutting trace to CW-EL-01\u201304 only when configured escalation changes task routing/responsibility": null, " otherwise N/A.": null}